[{:db/id "q-73335/selection/515199f58b4e2e21c809635c4c1e8c3b8633cb0321fc65bdb3ae6139119159f0" :answer/id #uuid "df7e3861-6845-507f-a3fe-2ab1edef4223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,v=-\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335/selection/8a260f71c79e5ee9dc069e42d719a756eadd4513fedb23c0ab86dbdeb70df807" :answer/id #uuid "4b9e018a-54ab-5d05-8046-62e2477ef1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,v=-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335/selection/27cab5f9a2637df63db2cf5b71c5d557c47b5183ab2e90797854dcc270f35005" :answer/id #uuid "8155132e-fb38-5ac5-a729-ddd6db4a43fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335/selection/411d22112e80cd380b86df35ceb90f37ad841097392359b2ebb683ce9f26a18b" :answer/id #uuid "69b7e53b-44b6-5593-8a6e-deb2504add7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2},\\,v=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{e}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335/selection/877e0d6e047b6867f71412923c728ddea6b40e5e8e1d048d876b0a80120131db" :answer/id #uuid "38f0227d-9324-56e2-bff3-5e9ab523f2f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=1,\\,v=\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bee01c62-f6b0-5470-ac4f-67bfcd38591e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73335/selection/8a260f71c79e5ee9dc069e42d719a756eadd4513fedb23c0ab86dbdeb70df807" :answer-field/choices ["q-73335/selection/515199f58b4e2e21c809635c4c1e8c3b8633cb0321fc65bdb3ae6139119159f0" "q-73335/selection/8a260f71c79e5ee9dc069e42d719a756eadd4513fedb23c0ab86dbdeb70df807" "q-73335/selection/27cab5f9a2637df63db2cf5b71c5d557c47b5183ab2e90797854dcc270f35005" "q-73335/selection/411d22112e80cd380b86df35ceb90f37ad841097392359b2ebb683ce9f26a18b" "q-73335/selection/877e0d6e047b6867f71412923c728ddea6b40e5e8e1d048d876b0a80120131db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73335" :question/id #uuid "f742d5d3-d314-55a4-a2e7-77b78815a252" :question/math-academy-id "q-73335" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=(t+1){e}^{-t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1){e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =-t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =(t-1){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =(t-1){e}^{-t} \\\\ t-1 & =0 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=1.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(1)=-1\\cdot {e}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{e}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73335/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73335"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection/2ca228050e90e261668f52d4458cbce05213280cf44da88ca3af60c01f3a1bba" :answer/id #uuid "d20b8dd4-3ddd-55b3-86fb-83375e88024f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection/920b57f45781b9cc270e8ab064584dbd9d7f521cb50e1bdecefad6891dc3538b" :answer/id #uuid "82692d2c-fd1e-5b01-b3cb-6c8a0df337ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,e)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection/34bcdb8eb98150bb82d79272d172d176adcd0b30ee6f28e696cfccce0346c968" :answer/id #uuid "a41cbfb8-13e7-5a6a-a618-8f4d2b734f6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection/c93276d45be71a05dadfa6e58f715ce4539f4cf3bdf9c96ffa5bf099dd56815f" :answer/id #uuid "327e9d84-65fe-5e64-abf1-9e0e1ec85e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{2}{e})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection/96e32d130802ad9e4284f78f1d20c5758da94e548a6a90c50aff6bfdfc98f63b" :answer/id #uuid "e2935a20-1892-5012-9267-697c870c8e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdadce8-c65a-5ba9-962b-2b2deff8f5d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109289/selection/34bcdb8eb98150bb82d79272d172d176adcd0b30ee6f28e696cfccce0346c968" :answer-field/choices ["q-109289/selection/2ca228050e90e261668f52d4458cbce05213280cf44da88ca3af60c01f3a1bba" "q-109289/selection/920b57f45781b9cc270e8ab064584dbd9d7f521cb50e1bdecefad6891dc3538b" "q-109289/selection/34bcdb8eb98150bb82d79272d172d176adcd0b30ee6f28e696cfccce0346c968" "q-109289/selection/c93276d45be71a05dadfa6e58f715ce4539f4cf3bdf9c96ffa5bf099dd56815f" "q-109289/selection/96e32d130802ad9e4284f78f1d20c5758da94e548a6a90c50aff6bfdfc98f63b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109289" :question/id #uuid "50f47d99-0d29-59c2-bb2e-982faa827891" :question/math-academy-id "q-109289" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ where $t>0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2}{2\\sqrt{t}} & <0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2 & <0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & <-2 \\\\ t & <{e}^{-2} \\\\ t & <\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $t\\in (0,\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109289/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109289"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection/920b57f45781b9cc270e8ab064584dbd9d7f521cb50e1bdecefad6891dc3538b" :answer/id #uuid "feb1851d-1cdc-5e66-b8be-5e49f929eb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,e)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" :answer/id #uuid "0b552bf9-1beb-5221-a168-63e371ef621b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection/d631d895fc796f7b1bf7f3916b5c9325ff8367d8e4d1df38aa2b41b81940876e" :answer/id #uuid "c3741a95-9af5-5d6c-82c3-c2495ede1033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{1}{e})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection/49dd955f7246aaaf8b0009bb70935ca10c0397c18703e7d61cbb9a56e3d7ae6f" :answer/id #uuid "82e30da0-c514-5d6b-a4f2-32b57f53eeab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection/96e32d130802ad9e4284f78f1d20c5758da94e548a6a90c50aff6bfdfc98f63b" :answer/id #uuid "13ed8951-f25a-51bc-80b8-2224b159127c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b305db0-a24f-59f4-9972-7b09dd35b380" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109290/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-109290/selection/920b57f45781b9cc270e8ab064584dbd9d7f521cb50e1bdecefad6891dc3538b" "q-109290/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" "q-109290/selection/d631d895fc796f7b1bf7f3916b5c9325ff8367d8e4d1df38aa2b41b81940876e" "q-109290/selection/49dd955f7246aaaf8b0009bb70935ca10c0397c18703e7d61cbb9a56e3d7ae6f" "q-109290/selection/96e32d130802ad9e4284f78f1d20c5758da94e548a6a90c50aff6bfdfc98f63b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109290" :question/id #uuid "2912d1ed-8c93-531d-8d23-8555cf0ff32d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109290" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=t{e}^{-t},$ where $t>0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =(1-t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ (1-t){e}^{-t} & <0 \\\\ 1-t & <0 \\\\ t & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $t\\in (1,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection/337871c4ded8b56d27da847dac48b5d852318639dc7a5676356beeacb3a5d3e8" :answer/id #uuid "22238f90-983a-58d5-871e-8fa1a5e45d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,v=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection/e3427781e70a2d1b808876cce6c526bd7be48594bd52dad92362fe49805142ad" :answer/id #uuid "4bb0bd13-8b0d-5477-b3ec-c01f9997fc98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{15}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection/46696b5f18bbc7afdc9b9f3cdb86f29fd173bd0b0400cd1896469fb5bb02d18e" :answer/id #uuid "583ab37d-d38a-563f-9e91-5b988ae778cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2,\\,v=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection/345365c355de120a46d8a696fb26df5506e0a31c24cbb1be4abe3740ccc1a9f6" :answer/id #uuid "63cd8d30-4646-5be8-a435-41eb7a14e022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{49}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection/0b12335919e50b6698ef6f571d6783502885f1498b10edff7f902d79221db5e7" :answer/id #uuid "2a6ae59a-ef01-59d9-be2a-45a738702684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5771e197-f85c-5afa-a2e0-a3495933c4d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109307/selection/345365c355de120a46d8a696fb26df5506e0a31c24cbb1be4abe3740ccc1a9f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-109307/selection/337871c4ded8b56d27da847dac48b5d852318639dc7a5676356beeacb3a5d3e8" "q-109307/selection/e3427781e70a2d1b808876cce6c526bd7be48594bd52dad92362fe49805142ad" "q-109307/selection/46696b5f18bbc7afdc9b9f3cdb86f29fd173bd0b0400cd1896469fb5bb02d18e" "q-109307/selection/345365c355de120a46d8a696fb26df5506e0a31c24cbb1be4abe3740ccc1a9f6" "q-109307/selection/0b12335919e50b6698ef6f571d6783502885f1498b10edff7f902d79221db5e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109307" :question/id #uuid "7704a427-55d1-5f8e-bf57-d941d8544127" :question/math-academy-id "q-109307" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=7{t}^{2}-{t}^{3},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =14t-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(14t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =14-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14-6t & =0 \\\\ -6t & =-14 \\\\ t & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=\\frac{7}{3}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{7}{3}) & =14(\\frac{7}{3})-3{(\\frac{7}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{98}{3}-\\frac{49}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109307/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335924/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "81d3254d-3bed-51d0-8297-233436b64199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335924/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a079644d-0ffe-5199-814c-409514ebc282" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335924/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-335924/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335924/field-2/edabb9555af51da592d186df32ddaa4851849ade10a22cdc9b3f9ad2db70153d" :answer/id #uuid "dd9a4b56-1f5c-5ae0-ba62-c83012a38d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\ln(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335924/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c87fac21-c636-55be-8f97-5c5744f6805a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335924/field-2/edabb9555af51da592d186df32ddaa4851849ade10a22cdc9b3f9ad2db70153d" :answer-field/choices ["q-335924/field-2/edabb9555af51da592d186df32ddaa4851849ade10a22cdc9b3f9ad2db70153d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335924" :question/id #uuid "32a4841d-90ea-5da4-90fb-13141a3fa68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335924" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)-{t}^{2},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}-2t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+1-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+1-2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a(t)=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}-2 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t} & =2 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\,(\\frac{1}{2}) & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2})+1-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2})+1-1 \\\\  & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=\\frac{1}{2},$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-335924/field-1" "q-335924/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335924"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
